A union a key-less fallback rule names, SetSessionConfigOptionRequest, decodes
a discriminator no variant names into its key-less variant when the payload
carries its keys and decodes as it, as the variant's description says, and
keeps it in Unknown otherwise. A union of the same shape that no rule names
keeps it in Unknown (0011-MADR-harden-code-generator-engine.md, F1;
0049-PLAN-surface-fixes.md, phase 1, deviation 2).
The meta declares $/cancel_request and the schema its smallest definition, which
the runtime needs.

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "SetSessionConfigOptionRequest": {"anyOf": [{"description": "A boolean value.", "type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "boolean"}, "value": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["type", "value"]}, {"title": "value_id", "description": "A string value.\n\nThis is the default when `type` is absent on the wire. Unknown `type`\nvalues with string payloads also gracefully deserialize into this\nvariant.", "type": "object", "properties": {"value": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["value"]}]},
  "V": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"type": "string", "const": "boolean"}, "value": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["type", "value"]}, {"title": "value_id", "type": "object", "properties": {"value": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["value"]}]},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
